      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i just updated the A records for our client's site but the new IP isnt showing up for me yet. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually work everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "DNS changes take time to propagate due to a system called DNS caching. When you update an A record, global servers around the world need to refresh their cached information before they start showing the new IP address. This propagation period can range from a few minutes to up to 48 hours, depending on various caching settings.",
