    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "is there anything i can do to speed it up? like is there a specific setting in the records that makes it update faster or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While you cannot instantly force every server to update, you can influence the speed by reducing the Time-To-Live (TTL) setting on your records. A lower TTL tells resolvers to cache the information for a shorter period, meaning they check back with your updated record more often. However, remember that lowering the TTL also increases DNS query traffic.",
      "source": "target",
