    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so random though. like sometimes it's instant and other times it's like the data is just... hiding or something. why is it so inconsistent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The inconsistency comes down to how many different caches are involved globally. Different ISPs, hosting providers, and even individual DNS resolvers cache your records at different times. Sometimes, the resolver nearest to you has just refreshed its cache, leading to an \"instant\" update, while others are still holding onto the old data.",
      "source": "target",
